WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:11.655
Today on Hey, Flag!, we have three special guests from North America.

2
00:00:11.656 --> 00:00:16.351
Hey, Flag! Tell us about yourself.

3
00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:18.617
"I am the Mexican flag.

4
00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.208
I have three stripes.

5
00:00:21.209 --> 00:00:24.098
The Mexican coat of arms is in the middle.

6
00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:28.148
The coat of arms has a very special meaning.

7
00:00:28.149 --> 00:00:34.411
It symbolizes the Aztec people who lived in Mexico long ago.

8
00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:38.959
"The coat of arms shows an eagle sitting on a cactus.

9
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.621
The eagle is eating a snake.

10
00:00:41.622 --> 00:00:46.331
This symbol came from an Aztec legend.

11
00:00:46.332 --> 00:00:50.914
The legend tells how Mexico City was founded.

12
00:00:50.915 --> 00:00:55.267
"There is a funny story about my red stripe.

13
00:00:55.268 --> 00:00:59.876
Originally the Mexican people wanted to use purple.

14
00:00:59.877 --> 00:01:05.671
Purple represented Spain, where most of Mexico's people came from.

15
00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:09.183
But they could not find any purple cloth.

16
00:01:09.184 --> 00:01:13.912
So they had to use red."

17
00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:18.617
Hey, Flag! Tell us about yourself.

18
00:01:18.618 --> 00:01:22.712
"I am the flag of the United States of America.

19
00:01:22.713 --> 00:01:26.105
Many people call me the Stars and Stripes.

20
00:01:26.106 --> 00:01:33.291
I have fifty stars, one for each of the states.

21
00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:39.205
I also have thirteen stripes for each of the original states.

22
00:01:39.206 --> 00:01:42.015
I didn't always have fifty stars.

23
00:01:42.016 --> 00:01:47.237
Every time a new state was added, I got another star.

24
00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:52.149
"Many people believe I was first sewn by Betsy Ross.

25
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:57.470
According to the story, George Washington asked Betsy to sew me.

26
00:01:57.471 --> 00:02:02.759
"The first flag was ready in early June 1776.

27
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:10.434
This was just a month before the United States became an independent country.

28
00:02:10.435 --> 00:02:16.493
"Many Americans see me as the greatest symbol of their nation."

29
00:02:16.494 --> 00:02:22.153
Hey, Flag! Tell us about yourself.

30
00:02:22.154 --> 00:02:27.606
"I am the Canadian flag. You can call me the Maple Leaf.

31
00:02:27.607 --> 00:02:32.484
I did not become the Canadian flag until 1965.

32
00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:36.849
Before that, Canadians used the flag of Great Britain.

33
00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:40.884
But the people of Canada wanted to have their own flag.

34
00:02:40.885 --> 00:02:45.861
"The maple leaf has been a symbol of Canada for a very long time.

35
00:02:45.862 --> 00:02:50.994
In 1860 the Prince of Wales came to Canada for a visit.

36
00:02:50.995 --> 00:02:56.504
Everyone in Toronto came out into the streets to greet him.

37
00:02:56.505 --> 00:03:01.342
"The people who were born in England wore a rose on their shirts.

38
00:03:01.343 --> 00:03:05.233
And the people born in Scotland wore a thistle.

39
00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:09.329
But there was nothing for the people born in Canada to wear.

40
00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:13.682
So they chose to wear a maple leaf from the Canadian maple tree.

41
00:03:13.683 --> 00:03:18.850
"From that day on, the maple leaf became a Canadian symbol."

42
00:03:18.851 --> 00:03:21.786
I hope you learned a lot from our guests.

43
00:03:21.787 --> 00:03:25.712
Your flag can tell you a lot about your country.

44
00:03:25.713 --> 00:03:34.328
What does your flag mean?

